Room: the hovered link of a page in a Room window goes to the host.

Chrome shows the link under the pointer in its status bubble:
BrowserWebContentsDelegate::UpdateTargetURL walks the window's status
bubbles and static_casts each one to StatusBubbleViews (and its anchor to
ContentsWebView). A Room window draws no Views, so RoomBrowserWindow
returns no status bubble (any other StatusBubble would be undefined
behaviour here and in ContentsMouseEvent), and without this hook the link
never reaches the host's status pill (didChangeStatusText, Phase 2.6b).

No existing hook: UpdateTargetURL is a WebContentsDelegate member only (no
WebContentsObserver event carries the hovered link), the tab's delegate is
Chrome's BrowserWebContentsDelegate, and a delegate wrapping it would have to
forward ~150 members.

Phase 3.2a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_web_contents.mm
(InstallWebContentsHooks).
